# GMS asks for a shield or a dagger scabbard in the off hand and grants DEF,
# avoidability, attack and damage reduction for it. The avoidability is left
# out: GMS grants a share of the AVOID STAT here, which is the accuracy check
# and not the flat roll dodge_chance models. See Illusion Step for the other
# kind.
#
# The rest is on GMS's own figures: DEF and the damage taken both 11% and 6% a
# level, and attack ending at its +20. All of it waits on the off hand. The DEF
# is worth nothing and is here for the figure -- see SkillEffect::def_pct.
name: "Shield Mastery"
description:
  "Increases DEF and Attack Power when a secondary weapon is equipped, and "
  "reduces damage taken."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_BANDIT skill_order: 8 }
max_level: 10
requires_secondary: true
base {
  damage_taken_pct: 0.06
  def_pct: 0.11
  attack: 2
}
per_level {
  damage_taken_pct: 0.06
  def_pct: 0.11
  attack: 2
}
